hashes are in `source-sha256.txt`. The final\\nfeature patch is `interval-breakdown.patch`. Unrelated stack-pool diagnostics\\nwere preserved.\\n\\n## Correctness changes\\n\\n- GPUFwd is the model-forward window again. Separate lm_head/logits timing does\\n  not extend the model tiling or count CPU collection as a GPU pipeline bubble.\\n- No per-forward device synchronization at compute_logits. Its events are read\\n  at the next existing model collection point, with two retained origin events.\\n  Only final shutdown drains the last pending logits measurement.\\n- Readiness comes from the actual CUDA event that the consumer waited on. Its\\n  existing record/wait is reused with timing enabled. Missing, shared/ambiguous,\\n  or subsequently re-recorded events remain unavailable; no producer proxy.\\n- Removed approximately 400 prefetch CUDA event records per 80-layer forward.\\n  Host issue observations remain, but no CPU/GPU clock subtraction or alleged\\n  queue delay is emitted.\\n- Numeric event snapshots are sent through a bounded queue to a CPU-only spool\\n  process. MessagePack serialization contains no executable pickle objects.\\n  During inference the worker only writes binary records. Interval analysis and\\n  CSV generation run after inference exits, automatically from both suites.\\n- Queue overflow, truncated output, worker failure and abnormal EOF invalidate\\n  the diagnostic run instead of silently dropping samples or blocking inference.\\n- Legacy aggregates and detailed capture reuse timestamp and interval reads.\\n\\n## Tests and actual flows\\n\\n18 tests passed; one opt-in full GPU feature matrix skipped. This includes the\\nrepository's lightweight feature-matrix contract test, affected KV-metrics tests,\\nand regression coverage for direct readiness, event reuse, clock separation,\\nmodel/logits scopes, cached clipping, shutdown drain and output backpressure.\\nSyntax/diff checks passed. Standards and requirements were reviewed directly.\\n\\nReal GH200/70B offline driver, CD3 fused + compressed KV, batch 16, input length\\n1020, generation 33, dedicated KV blocks 16, planner blocks 4096, first 4 decode\\nintervals excluded for the comparison. Same driver/options and fresh processes:\\n\\n| Warmed decode metric | Original breakdown | Corrected breakdown |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| TPOT mean | 132.95 ms | 138.30 ms |\\n| GPU model-forward mean | 93.1979 ms | 94.5436 ms |\\n\\nObserved differences: TPOT +4.02%, model-forward +1.44%. These are one paired\\ncomparison, not universal overhead bounds or an uninstrumented comparison.\\nThe previously delivered implementation had shown TPOT +18.97% in the earlier\\naudit. Added capture cost in the corrected run averaged about 2.73 ms/forward;\\nMessagePack enqueue cost about 0.32 ms/forward. The latter is measured outside\\nGPUFwd; neither metric includes all pre-existing breakdown costs.\\n\\nOffline recorded 34 complete model partitions and 34 separate logits intervals;\\nall 13,600 host prefetch observations were preserved. 13,598 waits had direct\\nreadiness timestamps; two prefill events re-recorded after their wait were NA.\\nModel state/region sums agreed with model-forward durations.\\n\\nReal serving suite `--smoke --breakdown`, CD3 kvcomp, chunk 8192, max-num-seqs 2,\\ndedicated KV blocks 16: two HTTP requests completed and the server shut down\\nnormally. The suite automatically converted and summarized snapshots. There were\\n127 complete model+logits forwards, 5,840 KV H2D windows covering 80 layers, and\\n50,800 host prefetch observations. Three re-recorded ready events were NA; all\\nother wait rows used direct events. Producer and worker both reported 127 frames,\\nzero drops, no errors. Exact-state sums agreed with GPUFwd. GPU/hugepage resources\\nreturned to idle and no output worker remained alive.\\n\\n## Limits\\n\\nThese are instrumented event-window measurements, not pure DMA/SM busy time or\\nzero-interference observations. Device event re